---
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '~/components/PageHero.astro';
import Icon from '~/components/ui/Icon.astro';

const UPDATED = 'July 28, 2026';

const REPORT_EMAIL = 'privacy@clientcove.io';

// Deliberately limited to the posture already stated publicly in the privacy
// policy. Operational specifics belong in the self-host documentation, not on a
// marketing page in a public repo.
const weOperate = [
  { t: 'clientcove.io', b: 'This marketing site. Static pages, no accounts, no customer data.' },
  { t: 'account.clientcove.io', b: 'Licence issuing and validation, and the OAuth broker for Google connections.' },
];

const weDont = [
  { t: 'Your portal', b: 'Runs on infrastructure you own or rent, on your domain.' },
  { t: 'Your database', b: 'Your clients, projects, files, invoices and any synced mail. We have no access to it.' },
  { t: 'Your backups', b: 'Yours to take, store and restore on your own schedule.' },
];
---
<Layout
  title="Security — How ClientCove is built and what we can and can't see"
  description="ClientCove is self-hosted: your portal and your database run on infrastructure you control. What we operate, what we don't, and how to report a vulnerability."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="SECURITY"
    title="We can't lose <em class='acc'>what we never hold.</em>"
    subtitle="ClientCove is self-hosted by design. Your database lives on your infrastructure, which changes what a compromise of ours could even reach."
  />

  <section class="sect" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container legal-wrap">
      <div class="legal-meta">
        <span><strong>Last updated</strong> {UPDATED}</span>
      </div>

      <div class="legal">
        <h2>The architecture is the control</h2>
        <p>
          Most client portals are multi-tenant: every customer's data sits in one provider's
          database, and that database becomes a single, very attractive target. ClientCove is
          licensed and self-hosted, so there is no such database. Each install is its own system, on
          its own infrastructure, under its owner's control.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is a genuine security property rather than a marketing line — but it moves
          responsibility as well as risk. We are responsible for the software and the small number of
          services we run. You are responsible for the server it runs on.
        </p>

        <h2>What we operate</h2>
        <ul class="split">
          {weOperate.map(x => <li><strong>{x.t}</strong><span>{x.b}</span></li>)}
        </ul>

        <h2>What we don't</h2>
        <ul class="split">
          {weDont.map(x => <li><strong>{x.t}</strong><span>{x.b}</span></li>)}
        </ul>

        <h2>Handling of connected accounts</h2>
        <p>
          Where the portal connects to an outside service on your behalf — a Google mailbox, for
          example — credentials are held on your install rather than centrally, and the broker that
          performs the authorisation exchange retains no tokens. The reasoning, and the specifics of
          what is stored and for how long, are set out in the
          <a href="/app/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
          clientcove.io runs no analytics, no advertising tags and no third-party tracking scripts,
          and sets no tracking cookies. There is no account system here and no customer data to
          expose.
        </p>

        <h2>Your side of it</h2>
        <p>
          Because you run the install, its security is yours to configure: the host, transport
          security, database access, backups, and who has administrative accounts. We publish
          hardening guidance in the
          <a href="https://docs.clientcove.io/self-host" rel="noopener">self-host playbook</a>, and
          support can help you work through it — but we cannot enforce it on infrastructure we do not
          operate, and we would rather say so plainly than imply otherwise.
        </p>

        <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            If you believe you have found a security issue in ClientCove, write to
            <a href={`mailto:${REPORT_EMAIL}`}>{REPORT_EMAIL}</a>. Include enough detail to
            reproduce it. We will acknowledge your report, keep you updated while we work on it, and
            credit you when a fix ships if you would like us to.
          </p>
          <p>
            Please give us a reasonable opportunity to fix an issue before disclosing it publicly. We
            will not pursue legal action against anyone who reports a genuine vulnerability in good
            faith and does not access, alter or destroy other people's data in the course of finding
            it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>No system is perfect</h2>
        <p>
          We do not claim ClientCove is unbreakable, and we are wary of vendors who do. What we can
          say is that the design deliberately avoids collecting things we would then have to protect,
          and that we would rather hold less of your data than promise to guard more of it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-cta">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark btn-lg">Contact the team <Icon name="arrow" class="arrow" /></a>
        <a href="/app/privacy-policy" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Privacy policy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-wrap { max-width: 820px; }

  .legal-meta {
    display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center;
    font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--color-ink-3);
    padding-bottom: 22px; margin-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .legal-meta strong { color: var(--color-ink-2); font-weight: 600; }

  .legal { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2); }
  .legal h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 27px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--color-ink); margin: 52px 0 16px;
  }
  .legal h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal p { margin: 0 0 16px; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .legal a { color: var(--color-orange-600); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(231,111,42,.3); }
  .legal a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--color-orange); }

  .split { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 16px; padding: 0; }
  .split li {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; gap: 18px;
    padding: 15px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line-2);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .split li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .split li strong { color: var(--color-ink); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13.5px; }

  .callout {
    background: var(--color-bg-2); border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 12px; padding: 26px 28px; margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .callout > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .legal-cta {
    display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 36px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .legal { font-size: 15.5px; }
    .legal h2 { font-size: 24px; margin-top: 42px; }
    .split li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }
  }
</style>
